# Browser security

- **[CSP-NONCE]** A strict Content-Security-Policy by nonce: no `unsafe-inline`, no `unsafe-eval`,
  no host wildcard. Every new third-party domain is added explicitly and justified.
- **[SECURITY-HEADERS]** `Strict-Transport-Security` (preloaded), `X-Content-Type-Options:
  nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, a minimal `Permissions-Policy`,
  `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`. Checked by a test.
- **[COOKIES]** Every session cookie is `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite=Lax` at least, and
  prefixed `__Host-` when it needs no subdomain.
- **[SUBRESOURCE-INTEGRITY]** No third-party script loaded from a CDN without Subresource
  Integrity.
